      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/mimagoniates_barberi_en/",
      "html": "<p>Mimagoniates barberi is a beautiful blue tetra from Paraguay and a very lively brook fish. Wild-collected fish seem to be fully grown; at least they are sexually ripe.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/mimagoniates_barberi_en/",
      "html": "<p>They are kept best at room temperature without an additional heater; however, they also accept water temperatures up to 26°C without feeling uncomfortable.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/mimagoniates_barberi_en/",
      "html": "<p>These animals are very peaceful schooling fish.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "dimorphism",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/mimagoniates_barberi_en/",
      "html": "<p>The males (about 4 cm total length) are larger and heavier built than the females.</p>"
